      "path": "index.html",
      "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Pixel 4x4 Sudoku</title>\n  <style>\n    [hidden] {\n      display: none !important;\n    }\n\n    :root {\n      --bg-color: #1a1c23;\n      --card-bg: #272a37;\n      --border-color: #3f4458;\n      --accent-color: #4ade80;\n      --text-color: #f3f4f6;\n      --text-muted: #9ca3af;\n      --error-color: #ef4444;\n      --error-bg: #451a1a;\n      --prefilled-bg: #323647;\n      --cell-bg: #1f222d;\n      --focus-ring: #60a5fa;\n    }\n\n    * {\n      box-sizing: border-box;\n      margin: 0;\n      padding: 0;\n    }\n\n    body {\n      min-height: 100vh;\n      background-color: var(--bg-color);\n      color: var(--text-color);\n      font-family: ui-monospace, 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;\n      font-size: 16px;\n      display: flex;\n      flex-direction: column;\n      align-items: center;\n      justify-content: center;\n      padding: 16px;\n    }\n\n    .game-card {\n      background: var(--card-bg);\n      border: 4px solid var(--border-color);\n      box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #0d0e12;\n      border-radius: 4px;\n      padding: 24px;\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 420px;\n      display: flex;\n      flex-direction: column;\n      align-items: center;\n      gap: 18px;\n    }\n\n    header {\n      text-align: center;\n    }\n\n    h1 {\n      font-size: 1.6rem;\n      letter-spacing: 2px;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      color: var(--accent-color);\n      margin-bottom: 6px;\n      text-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #000;\n    }\n\n    .instructions {\n      font-size: 0.85rem;\n      color: var(--text-muted);\n      line-height: 1.4;\n    }\n\n    .status-area {\n      min-height: 38px;\n      display: flex;\n      align-items: center;\n      justify-content: center;\n      width: 100%;\n    }\n\n    .status-msg {\n      font-size: 1.15rem;\n      font-weight: bold;\n      padding: 6px 14px;\n      border: 2px solid transparent;\n      text-align: center;\n    }\n\n    .status-msg.victory {\n      color: #000;\n      background-color: var(--accent-color);\n      border-color: #22c55e;\n      box-shadow: 3px 3px 0px #15803d;\n      animation: pulse 1s infinite alternate;\n    }\n\n    @keyframes pulse {\n      from { transform: scale(1); }\n      to { transform: scale(1.04); }\n    }\n\n    .board {\n      display: grid;\n      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);\n      gap: 4px;\n      background-color: var(--border-color);\n      border: 4px solid var(--border-color);\n      padding: 4px;\n      width: 100%;\n      aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;\n      max-width: 320px;\n    }\n\n    .cell {\n      position: relative;\n      display: flex;\n      align-items: center;\n      justify-content: center;\n      background: var(--cell-bg);\n      border: 2px solid transparent;\n    }\n\n    /* Visual border separators for 2x2 boxes */\n    .cell:nth-child(4n + 2) {\n      margin-right: 4px;\n    }\n    .cell:nth-child(n + 5):nth-child(-n + 8) {\n      margin-bottom: 4px;\n    }\n\n    .cell input {\n      width: 100%;\n      height: 100%;\n      background: transparent;\n      border: none;\n      text-align: center;\n      font-family: inherit;\n      font-size: 1.75rem;\n      font-weight: bold;\n      color: var(--text-color);\n      caret-color: var(--accent-color);\n      outline: none;\n      cursor: pointer;\n    }\n\n    .cell input:focus-visible {\n      background: rgba(96, 165, 250, 0.15);\n      box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--focus-ring);\n    }\n\n    .cell.prefilled {\n      background: var(--prefilled-bg);\n    }\n\n    .cell.prefilled input {\n      color: #93c5fd;\n      cursor: not-allowed;\n    }\n\n    .cell.conflict {\n      background-color: var(--error-bg) !important;\n      border-color: var(--error-color) !important;\n      box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--error-color);\n    }\n\n    .cell.conflict input {\n      color: var(--error-color) !important;\n    }\n\n    .controls {\n      display: flex;\n      gap: 12px;\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 320px;\n    }\n\n    .btn {\n      flex: 1;\n      background: #374151;\n      color: var(--text-color);\n      border: 2px solid #4b5563;\n      padding: 10px 16px;\n      font-family: inherit;\n      font-size: 0.95rem;\n      font-weight: bold;\n      cursor: pointer;\n      box-shadow: 3px 3px 0px #1f2937;\n      transition: transform 0.05s, box-shadow 0.05s;\n    }\n\n    .btn:hover {\n      background: #4b5563;\n    }\n\n    .btn:focus-visible {\n      outline: 2px solid var(--focus-ring);\n      outline-offset: 2px;\n    }\n\n    .btn:active {\n      transform: translate(2px, 2px);\n      box-shadow: 1px 1px 0px #1f2937;\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"game-card\">\n    <header>\n      <h1>Pixel 4x4</h1>\n      <p class=\"instructions\">Fill digits 1–4. Duplicates in row, col, or 2x2 box turn red.</p>\n    </header>\n\n    <div class=\"status-area\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n      <div id=\"status\" class=\"status-msg\" hidden>Solved!</div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div id=\"board\" class=\"board\" role=\"grid\" aria-label=\"4x4 Sudoku Grid\"></div>\n\n    <div class=\"controls\">\n      <button id=\"btn-reset\" class=\"btn\" type=\"button\">Reset</button>\n      <button id=\"btn-clear\" class=\"btn\" type=\"button\">Clear Inputs</button>\n    </div>\n  </main>\n\n  <script>\n    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {\n      // 0 represents empty editable cell\n      const INITIAL_PUZZLE = [\n        1, 0, 0, 4,\n        0, 0, 1, 0,\n        0, 1, 0, 0,\n        4, 0, 0, 2\n      ];\n\n      const boardEl = document.getElementById('board');\n      const statusEl = document.getElementById('status');\n      const btnReset = document.getElementById('btn-reset');\n      const btnClear = document.getElementById('btn-clear');\n\n      const cellElements = [];\n      const inputElements = [];\n\n      function initBoard() {\n        boardEl.innerHTML = '';\n        cellElements.length = 0;\n        inputElements.length = 0;\n\n        for (let i = 0; i < 16; i++) {\n          const row = Math.floor(i / 4);\n          const col = i % 4;\n          const isPrefilled = INITIAL_PUZZLE[i] !== 0;\n\n          const cell = document.createElement('div');\n          cell.className = 'cell' + (isPrefilled ? ' prefilled' : '');\n          cell.setAttribute('role', 'gridcell');\n\n          const input = document.createElement('input');\n          input.type = 'text';\n          input.inputMode = 'numeric';\n          input.maxLength = 1;\n          input.setAttribute('aria-label', `Row ${row + 1}, Column ${col + 1}`);\n          input.dataset.index = i;\n\n          if (isPrefilled) {\n            input.value = INITIAL_PUZZLE[i];\n            input.readOnly = true;\n            input.tabIndex = -1;\n          } else {\n            input.addEventListener('keydown', handleKeyNavigation);\n            input.addEventListener('input', handleCellInput);\n          }\n\n          cell.appendChild(input);\n          boardEl.appendChild(cell);\n\n          cellElements.push(cell);\n          inputElements.push(input);\n        }\n\n        validateBoard();\n      }\n\n      function handleKeyNavigation(e) {\n        const index = parseInt(e.target.dataset.index, 10);\n        let nextIndex = index;\n\n        if (e.key === 'ArrowUp') nextIndex = index - 4;\n        else if (e.key === 'ArrowDown') nextIndex = index + 4;\n        else if (e.key === 'ArrowLeft') nextIndex = index - 1;\n        else if (e.key === 'ArrowRight') nextIndex = index + 1;\n        else if (e.key === 'Backspace' || e.key === 'Delete') {\n          e.target.value = '';\n          validateBoard();\n          return;\n        } else {\n          return;\n        }\n\n        if (nextIndex >= 0 && nextIndex < 16) {\n          e.preventDefault();\n          inputElements[nextIndex].focus();\n        }\n      }\n\n      function handleCellInput(e) {\n        const val = e.target.value;\n        if (!['1', '2', '3', '4'].includes(val)) {\n          e.target.value = '';\n        }\n        validateBoard();\n      }\n\n      function validateBoard() {\n        const values = inputElements.map(inp => parseInt(inp.value, 10) || 0);\n        const conflicts = new Set();\n\n        // Check Rows\n        for (let r = 0; r < 4; r++) {\n          const seen = {};\n          for (let c = 0; c < 4; c++) {\n            const idx = r * 4 + c;\n            const val = values[idx];\n            if (val > 0) {\n              if (seen[val] !== undefined) {\n                conflicts.add(seen[val]);\n                conflicts.add(idx);\n              } else {\n                seen[val] = idx;\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        }\n\n        // Check Columns\n        for (let c = 0; c < 4; c++) {\n          const seen = {};\n          for (let r = 0; r < 4; r++) {\n            const idx = r * 4 + c;\n            const val = values[idx];\n            if (val > 0) {\n              if (seen[val] !== undefined) {\n                conflicts.add(seen[val]);\n                conflicts.add(idx);\n              } else {\n                seen[val] = idx;\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        }\n\n        // Check 2x2 Boxes\n        const boxStartIndices = [0, 2, 8, 10];\n        for (const start of boxStartIndices) {\n          const seen = {};\n          const boxOffsets = [0, 1, 4, 5];\n          for (const offset of boxOffsets) {\n            const idx = start + offset;\n            const val = values[idx];\n            if (val > 0) {\n              if (seen[val] !== undefined) {\n                conflicts.add(seen[val]);\n                conflicts.add(idx);\n              } else {\n                seen[val] = idx;\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        }\n\n        // Highlight conflicting cells\n        for (let i = 0; i < 16; i++) {\n          if (conflicts.has(i)) {\n            cellElements[i].classList.add('conflict');\n          } else {\n            cellElements[i].classList.remove('conflict');\n          }\n        }\n\n        // Check win state: completely filled with no duplicates\n        const isComplete = values.every(v => v >= 1 && v <= 4);\n        if (isComplete && conflicts.size === 0) {\n          statusEl.textContent = 'Solved!';\n          statusEl.className = 'status-msg victory';\n          statusEl.removeAttribute('hidden');\n        } else {\n          statusEl.setAttribute('hidden', '');\n          statusEl.className = 'status-msg';\n        }\n      }\n\n      btnReset.addEventListener('click', () => {\n        initBoard();\n        const firstEditable = inputElements.find(inp => !inp.readOnly);\n        if (firstEditable) firstEditable.focus();\n      });\n\n      btnClear.addEventListener('click', () => {\n        for (let i = 0; i < 16; i++) {\n          if (INITIAL_PUZZLE[i] === 0) {\n            inputElements[i].value = '';\n          }\n        }\n        validateBoard();\n        const firstEditable = inputElements.find(inp => !inp.readOnly);\n        if (firstEditable) firstEditable.focus();\n      });\n\n      initBoard();\n    });\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
      "description": "Main entry point containing the game markup, embedded pixel CSS styling, and complete 4x4 Sudoku logic."
    },
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel 4x4 Sudoku\n\nA responsive, offline 4x4 Sudoku game built with vanilla HTML, CSS, and JavaScript featuring instant conflict detection and a pixel aesthetic.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Built-in Puzzle**: Starts with pre-filled clues and editable empty cells.\n- **Instant Error Feedback**: Any cell that repeats a digit (1-4) in its row, column, or 2x2 box instantly turns red.\n- **Win State Detection**: Displays an animated **\"Solved!\"** banner once the entire grid is correctly filled without conflicts.\n- **Accessible Controls & Keyboard Navigation**: Arrow keys navigate across cells, numeric keys insert 1–4, and Delete/Backspace clears values.\n- **Pure Offline Architecture**: Zero dependencies, no network requests, and self-contained styling with `[hidden] { display: none !important; }` support.\n\n## Running the Game\n\nSimply open `index.html` in any modern web browser.\n",
      "description": "Project documentation explaining how to run the game, gameplay rules, and implementation details."
    }
  ]
}